info.description:
Collections API of a Qdrant serverless space.

A serverless space exposes the regular Qdrant API for points and search. Collections, however, are managed through this
simplified API: instead of HNSW, quantization and storage parameters you describe *what* the collection holds (dense and
sparse vectors, which payload fields you filter on, and how much precision you are willing to trade for cost). The
serverless manager turns that into concrete Qdrant settings.

Every request names the collection by its tenant-facing name. The tenant (account and space) is derived from the API key
and never appears in URLs or payloads.

## Examples

### Create a collection

```
curl -X PUT 'https://<your-space-endpoint>/collections/documents' \
  -H 'api-key: <YOUR_SPACE_API_KEY>' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  --data-raw '{
    "vectors": {
      "text": { "size": 1024, "distance": "Cosine", "precision": "medium" }
    },
    "sparse_vectors": {
      "bm25": { "modifier": "idf" }
    },
    "payload_indexes": {
      "user_id": "keyword",
      "created_at": "datetime",
      "title": { "type": "text", "tokenizer": "word", "stopwords": "english" }
    }
  }'
```

Expected response:

```
{
  "result": { "name": "documents", "created": true },
  "status": "ok",
  "time": 0.031
}
```

### Inspect it

```
curl 'https://<your-space-endpoint>/collections/documents' \
  -H 'api-key: <YOUR_SPACE_API_KEY>'
```

Expected response:

```
{
  "result": {
    "name": "documents",
    "config": {
      "vectors": {
        "text": { "size": 1024, "distance": "Cosine", "multivector": false, "precision": "medium" }
      },
      "sparse_vectors": {
        "bm25": { "modifier": "idf", "precision": "high" }
      },
      "payload_indexes": {
        "user_id": { "type": "keyword", "prefix": false },
        "created_at": { "type": "datetime" },
        "title": { "type": "text", "tokenizer": "word", "lowercase": true, "phrase_matching": true, "ascii_folding": false, "stopwords": { "languages": ["english"] } }
      }
    },
    "points_count": 0
  },
  "status": "ok",
  "time": 0.004
}
```

### List collections, page by page

```
curl 'https://<your-space-endpoint>/collections?limit=2' \
  -H 'api-key: <YOUR_SPACE_API_KEY>'
```

```
{
  "result": {
    "collections": [
      { "name": "documents", "points_count": 12873 },
      { "name": "images", "points_count": 4096 }
    ],
    "next_page_offset": "eyJsYXN0IjoiaW1hZ2VzIn0"
  },
  "status": "ok",
  "time": 0.003
}
```

Then `GET /collections?limit=2&offset=eyJsYXN0IjoiaW1hZ2VzIn0` for the next page; `next_page_offset` is `null` on the last one.

### Delete it

```
curl -X DELETE 'https://<your-space-endpoint>/collections/documents' \
  -H 'api-key: <YOUR_SPACE_API_KEY>'
```

```
{ "result": true, "status": "ok", "time": 0.12 }
```
